  "sourceSummary": "CriticalBody original Cable Concentration Curl by Liam Brown, seated protocol: flat bench opposite low cable column, straight bar underhand grip, bend over and brace backs of upperarms against knees, curl toward front delts then controlled return near full extension. This implements bilateral seated bar version, not unilateral standing variants. Brief0.4second peak within8second cycle is editorial rather than literal1second source hold.",
  "motion": "Seated bilateral cable concentration curl with55degree forward trunk lean, thighs spread and backs of upperarms braced at inner knees. Fixed torso/upperarms/feet, supinated straight bar with central ring and conserved continuous cable to low pulley and moving stack. Generic tower has extended user-side low pulley and floor return idler before upper pulley; this is procedural equipment, not a commercial replica. No preacher pad. Near-extension start to deep elbow flexion, actual smooth cycle.",
